          {
            "title": "Constructor",
            "id": 88767,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Esiste un metodo che possiamo usare, più flessibile per creare diverse istanze da una classe. Si chiama metodo <strong>constructor</strong>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, color)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.color = color\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"rocky = Virtual_Pet(\" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"benny = Virtual_Pet(\" /><text value=\"&quot;black&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(rocky.color)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(benny.color)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"brown\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"black\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Constructor",
            "id": 89355,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Il metodo costruttore è simile a <code>__init__()</code> e ci permette di impostare valori univoci per le variabili di classe quando creiamo un'istanza.</p><p>Assicurati di usare due caratteri di sottolineatura su entrambi i lati di <code>init</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, color)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.color = color\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"rocky = Virtual_Pet(\" /><text value=\"&quot;red&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"33\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>__init__</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Constructor",
            "id": 89359,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Invece di una definizione di classe che avrà sempre lo stesso colore, un metodo costruttore ci permette di specificare ciò che vogliamo quando la creiamo.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, color)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.color = color\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"rocky = Virtual_Pet(\" /><text value=\"&quot;red&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Constructor",
            "id": 89360,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando creiamo un'istanza dalla definizione della classe, possiamo passare valori unici tra le parentesi, come <code>yellow</code> qui.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, color)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.color = color\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"rocky = Virtual_Pet(\" /><text value=\"&quot;yellow&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"92\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"99\" /><option startIndex=\"99\" endIndex=\"100\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"</code>, seguito da <code>yellow</code> e infine <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Quando creiamo un'istanza dalla definizione della classe, possiamo passare valori univoci tra parentesi.</p><p>Crea <code>rocky</code> come nuova istanza contenente il colore <code>\"yellow\"</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(self, color)\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"    self.color = color\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"rocky = Virtual_Pet(\" /><text value=\"&quot;yellow&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"91\" /><option startIndex=\"91\" endIndex=\"92\" /><option startIndex=\"92\" endIndex=\"100\" /><option startIndex=\"100\" endIndex=\"101\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"rocky\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;red&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>Virtual_Pet</code>, seguito da <code>(</code>, <code>\"yellow\"</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Constructor",
            "id": 89354,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per aggiungere questa flessibilità alle nostre classi, iniziamo aggiungendo la funzione di costruzione, che ha questo aspetto: <code>__init__()</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"()\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"35\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>__init__</code>, seguito da <code>(</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per aggiungere questa flessibilità alle nostre classi, iniziamo aggiungendo la funzione di costruzione, che ha questo aspetto: <code>__init__()</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"def\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"__init__\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"()\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\":\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"21\" endIndex=\"24\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"33\" /><option startIndex=\"33\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"34\" endIndex=\"35\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"class\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Virtual_Pet\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>def</code>, seguito da <code>__init__</code>, <code>(</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
